{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Understand how TWS passes messages between your web content and native iOS code, and how to add a bridge of your own.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS\/01_Customizations"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS\/00_GettingStarted","doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS\/01_Customizations","doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS\/02_FileDownloads","doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS\/03_GoogleLogin"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"JavaScript bridges","modules":[{"name":"TWS"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS\/04_JavaScriptBridges","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A web view cannot call Swift directly, and Swift cannot call into a page directly. WebKit provides two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one-way pipes instead, and every bridge in TWS is built from the same pair:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"JS → native","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — the page calls "},{"code":"window.webkit.messageHandlers.<channel>.postMessage(payload)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"object conforming to "},{"code":"WKScriptMessageHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", registered under that channel name, receives it."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"native → JS","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Swift calls "},{"code":"evaluateJavaScript(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to invoke a function the page has defined."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"postMessage","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns nothing, so a bridge that needs an answer cannot simply wait for one. Where TWS needs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a round trip it sends a request id along with the message and calls back into a JavaScript function with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that same id, letting the JS side match the response to the caller that is waiting for it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Both halves are wired up in ","type":"text"},{"code":"makeUIView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on a single ","type":"text"},{"code":"WKUserContentController","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shared by the web view: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"JavaScript side is injected as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"WKUserScript","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" at ","type":"text"},{"code":".atDocumentStart","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so it exists before any page code","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"runs, and the native side is registered with ","type":"text"},{"code":"add(_:name:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"1-Built-in-bridges","text":"1. Built-in bridges","type":"heading"},{"level":3,"anchor":"11-intercept-SPA-navigation","text":"1.1 `intercept` — SPA navigation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The only built-in channel with no injected script: the channel exists, and it is up to your web content to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use it. When a single-page app changes route without a page load, the page tells the host:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"js","code":["window.webkit.messageHandlers.intercept.postMessage(\"\/some\/path\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SPAInterceptorBridge","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" receives it and forwards it to your "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS\/TWSViewInterceptor"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS\/TWSIntercepted\/path(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":". The channel is registered only when an interceptor is bound to the view."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Unlike ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS\/TWSIntercepted\/url(_:navigationType:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", the return value of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"handleIntercept(_:)"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"discarded for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".path"},{"text":". A full page load can be vetoed because the interceptor runs inside the navigation","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"policy decision; an SPA route change has already happened by the time JavaScript reports it, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".path"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a notification rather than a veto.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"1.2 `locationHandler` — geolocation","level":3,"anchor":"12-locationHandler-geolocation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The most complete bridge, and the best model to copy. The injected script replaces the standard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"navigator.geolocation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" functions, so page code keeps using the ordinary Web API and never learns it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"talking to native code.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each call mints a unique id, stores the page’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"success","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" callbacks against it, and posts a JSON"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"payload:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"js","code":["navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition = function(success, error, options) {","    const id = Date.now();","    locationCallbacks.set(id, { success, error });","    window.webkit.messageHandlers.locationHandler.postMessage(","        JSON.stringify({ id: id, command: \"getCurrentPosition\", options: options })","    );","};"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Native decodes the payload, asks the bound "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocationServicesBridge"},{"type":"text","text":" for a fix, and replies by calling one of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the functions the same script defined — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"navigator.geolocation.iosLastLocation(id, lat, lon, …)"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iosWatchLocationDidUpdate(…)"},{"text":", or their ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"…Failed"},{"text":" counterparts. The JS side looks the id up and invokes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stored callback.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two details are worth borrowing. The id is ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date.now()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rather than a counter, because several web views may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"share one location provider and a per-view counter would collide. And the message handler itself holds no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state: it keeps a static list of ","type":"text"},{"code":"JavaScriptLocationAdapter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" actors and broadcasts to them, because a message","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler is retained by the content controller and storing the web view on it would create a retain cycle.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The adapter holds the web view and the services bridge weakly.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"13-consoleLogHandler-console-forwarding","type":"heading","text":"1.3 `consoleLogHandler` — console forwarding"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Compiled in ","type":"text"},{"code":"#if DEBUG","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only. The injected script wraps ","type":"text"},{"code":"console.log","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"warn","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"info","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"debug","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"posts ","type":"text"},{"code":"{type, timestamp, args}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the channel, then calls the original implementation so the browser console","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"still works. Native writes the result to the TWS log, which is how web console output reaches Xcode.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"2-Native-%E2%86%92-JS-without-a-channel","type":"heading","text":"2. Native → JS without a channel"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Not every native-to-web call needs a registered handler. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS\/TWSViewNavigator"},{"text":"’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS\/TWSViewNavigator\/pushState(path:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS\/TWSViewNavigator\/replaceState(path:)"},{"text":" are plain","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"evaluateJavaScript","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" calls. They first feature-check the page:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"js","code":["typeof window.navigateFromNative === 'function'"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If your web content defines ","type":"text"},{"code":"navigateFromNative(path, { replace })","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", TWS calls it and lets your router","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handle the change. If not, it falls back to ","type":"text"},{"code":"history.pushState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"replaceState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" followed by a synthetic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"popstate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" event. Defining ","type":"text"},{"code":"navigateFromNative","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is preferable — the fallback works only for routers that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"listen to ","type":"text"},{"code":"popstate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"3-Lifecycle","type":"heading","text":"3. Lifecycle"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Handlers are registered per web view in ","type":"text"},{"code":"makeUIView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and torn down in ","type":"text"},{"code":"dismantleUIView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which calls","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"removeAllScriptMessageHandlers()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Note the “all”: it clears channels you registered yourself alongside the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"built-in ones.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A new web view — and therefore a fresh set of handlers — is created whenever the view’s identity changes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not once per app launch. Web views opened as popups through the ","type":"text"},{"code":"WKUIDelegate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are separate instances with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their own registrations.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"4-Adding-your-own-bridge","type":"heading","text":"4. Adding your own bridge"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS\/TWSView\/init(snippet:state:overrides:overrideVisibilty:enablePullToRefresh:onCreate:)"},{"text":" to get hold of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"code":"WKWebView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as it is created, then register a channel on its content controller:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["final class GreetingBridge: NSObject, WKScriptMessageHandler {","    func userContentController(","        _ userContentController: WKUserContentController,","        didReceive message: WKScriptMessage","    ) {","        guard message.name == \"greeting\", let name = message.body as? String else { return }","        print(\"Hello, \\(name)!\")","    }","}","","TWSView(snippet: snippet, onCreate: { webView in","    webView.configuration.userContentController.add(GreetingBridge(), name: \"greeting\")","})"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the channel needs a JavaScript counterpart, add it as a user script at the same time so it is in place","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before page code runs:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["webView.configuration.userContentController.addUserScript(","    WKUserScript(source: js, injectionTime: .atDocumentStart, forMainFrameOnly: true)",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"onCreate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs after TWS has registered its own channels and before the first content load, so user","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scripts added here still apply to that load, and a channel name TWS already uses will fail loudly rather","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than silently — ","type":"text"},{"code":"add(_:name:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" raises an exception on a duplicate name.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Three things to avoid. Do not reassign ","type":"text"},{"code":"navigationDelegate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"uiDelegate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — TWS sets both to its own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"coordinator and replacing either disables navigation handling, interception, downloads and permissions.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Do not load content, since the snippet’s own first load follows immediately and will replace it. And","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"remember that ","type":"text"},{"code":"onCreate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs for every web view the view creates, so a handler that registers external","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state should tolerate being set up more than once.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tws\/04_javascriptbridges"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://tws-ios.TWS/documentation/TWS":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS\/documentation\/TWS","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Transform Your Website into a Powerful Mobile App in Minutes.","type":"text"}],"images":[{"type":"icon","identifier":"appIcon-200x200.png"}],"title":"TWS","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tws"},"appIcon-200x200.png":{"variants":[{"url":"\/images\/tws-ios.TWS\/appIcon-200x200.png","traits":["1x","light"]}],"type":"image","alt":"TWS Logo","identifier":"appIcon-200x200.png"},"doc://tws-ios.TWS/documentation/TWS/TWSView/init(snippet:state:overrides:overrideVisibilty:enablePullToRefresh:onCreate:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/tws\/twsview\/init(snippet:state:overrides:overridevisibilty:enablepulltorefresh:oncreate:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Main contructor","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"snippet","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TWSSnippet","preciseIdentifier":"s:9TWSModels10TWSSnippetV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"state","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bindable","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI8BindableV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"TWSViewState","preciseIdentifier":"s:3TWS12TWSViewStateC","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"overrides","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"TWSRawDynamicResource","preciseIdentifier":"s:9TWSModels21TWSRawDynamicResourceO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"], ","kind":"text"},{"text":"overrideVisibilty","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enablePullToRefresh","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"onCreate","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (@","kind":"text"},{"text":"MainActor","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"text":"WKWebView","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)WKWebView"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Void","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida"},{"text":")?)","kind":"text"}],"title":"init(snippet:state:overrides:overrideVisibilty:enablePullToRefresh:onCreate:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/tws-ios.TWS